<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>History Shorts Kit — Built by Bots Store</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Mono:wght@400;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/amiga.css">
<script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead2/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-2874546800688654" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script defer data-domain="builtbybots.show" src="https://stats.eonic.cloud/js/script.outbound-links.js"></script>
<style>
.kit-hero{padding:80px 0 40px;text-align:center}
.kit-hero h1{font-size:2.4em;color:var(--glow);margin-bottom:12px}
.kit-hero .tagline{font-size:1.15em;color:var(--fg2);max-width:600px;margin:0 auto 24px;line-height:1.6}
.kit-hero .price{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:2em;color:var(--glow);margin:20px 0 8px}
.kit-hero .price-note{font-size:.85em;color:var(--fg3)}

.episode-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:20px;margin:40px 0}
.ep-card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:2px;padding:20px;transition:border-color .2s}
.ep-card:hover{border-color:var(--glow)}
.ep-num{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.75em;color:var(--glow);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px}
.ep-card h3{font-size:1.05em;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 6px;line-height:1.3}
.ep-punchline{font-size:.88em;color:var(--fg2);line-height:1.5;margin:0}
.ep-punchline em{color:var(--glow2);font-style:normal}

.section-title{font-size:1.6em;color:var(--glow);margin:48px 0 16px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.section-title .eyebrow{display:block;font-size:.7em;color:var(--fg3);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px}

.feature-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px;margin:24px 0}
.feature{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:20px;border-radius:2px}
.feature h4{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.95em;color:var(--glow);margin:0 0 8px}
.feature p{font-size:.88em;color:var(--fg2);line-height:1.6;margin:0}

.cta-section{text-align:center;padding:60px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:48px}
.cta-section h2{font-size:2em;color:var(--glow);margin-bottom:12px}
.cta-section p{color:var(--fg2);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 24px;line-height:1.6}
.cta-section .price{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:2.2em;color:var(--glow);margin:20px 0}
.cta-section .price-note{font-size:.85em;color:var(--fg3);margin-bottom:24px}

.testimonial{background:var(--card);border-left:3px solid var(--glow);padding:20px 24px;margin:32px 0;border-radius:0 2px 2px 0}
.testimonial p{font-size:.95em;color:var(--fg2);line-height:1.7;margin:0}
.testimonial .attribution{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8em;color:var(--fg3);margin-top:8px}

.aria-banner{position:sticky;top:56px;z-index:40;background:var(--purple);color:var(--bg);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.85em;text-align:center;padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.aria-banner a{color:var(--bg);font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline}
.aria-banner strong{color:var(--bg)}

@media(max-width:640px){
  .kit-hero h1{font-size:1.7em}
  .kit-hero .price{font-size:1.6em}
  .episode-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .feature-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .aria-banner{font-size:.75em;padding:8px 12px}
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header><div class="wrap"><nav>
  <a class="brand" href="/">BUILT BY BOTS<span class="dot">.</span></a>
  <div class="navlinks">
    <a href="/blog/" class="hidesm">Blog</a>
    <a href="/episodes/">Episodes</a>
    <a href="/arcade/" style="color:var(--glow)">Arcade</a>
    <a href="/aria/" style="color:var(--purple2)">Aria</a>
    <a href="/store/" style="color:var(--glow)">Store</a>
    <a href="https://www.patreon.com/builtbybots" class="btn btn-primary">Patreon</a>
  </div>
</nav></div></header>

<div class="aria-banner"><div class="wrap">🤖 Also want <strong>Your Own AI</strong>? Aria answers your phone, books appointments, and works 24/7 — from $49/mo. <a href="/aria/">See plans →</a></div></div>

<div class="kit-hero"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--fg3);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8em;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:12px">▸ The first Built by Bots product</div>
  <h1>History Shorts Kit</h1>
  <p class="tagline">24 dithered history shorts. Every script, every production note, every image source, and the complete Amiga pipeline spec. Buy once, use forever. Render them yourself, or just read them for the stories.</p>
  <div class="price">$29</div>
  <div class="price-note">Digital download · No subscription · 100% direct — no marketplace cut</div>
</div></div>

<section class="wrap">
<div class="section-title"><span class="eyebrow">All 24 Episodes</span>What You Get</div>

<div class="episode-grid">

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #01</div>
  <h3>The Metal Detector President</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Garfield was shot. Bell invented the metal detector to save him. He failed. <em>"The thing beeping at you in airport security exists because a president got shot and the inventor of the telephone tried to save his life."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #02</div>
  <h3>The Greenback</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Lincoln printed paper money to fund a war with empty gold reserves. <em>"The green in 'greenback' isn't economics. It's inventory."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #03</div>
  <h3>The Container That Changed the World</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">One truck driver got sick of waiting and invented the shipping container. <em>"He's the reason your phone costs $999 instead of $9,999."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #04</div>
  <h3>The Woman Who Mapped the Floor</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Marie Tharp discovered plate tectonics. A man got credit for 40 years. <em>"Bad luck on ships. Good luck for science."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #05</div>
  <h3>The Town They Buried</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">The government sprayed a Missouri town with poison, then bought it and buried it. <em>"They paved the town with poison. Then they paved over the town."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #06</div>
  <h3>The Day the Music Changed</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">A senator's wife heard a Prince song. The parental advisory sticker was born. <em>"They tried to put a warning label on culture. Culture put a price tag on the warning."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #07</div>
  <h3>The Microwave That Melted a Candy Bar</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">A radar engineer's chocolate bar melted near a magnetron. <em>"Sometimes the biggest discoveries start with 'huh.'"</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #08</div>
  <h3>The Barcode That Ate the World</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">A grad student drew lines in the sand on a Miami beach. <em>"Next time you hear that beep, remember: it started on a beach."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #09</div>
  <h3>The QR Code That Wasn't About Payments</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Invented to track car parts. Given away for free. <em>"The fastest response in history started with the slowest assembly line."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #10</div>
  <h3>The Elevator That Made Cities</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Otis cut the rope and the crowd gasped. The platform stopped. <em>"All safe, gentlemen. All safe."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #11</div>
  <h3>The Time Zone That Built the Railroad</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Trains kept crashing because every town had its own clock. One engineer fixed time itself. <em>"The world agreed on time because the world couldn't agree on clocks."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #12</div>
  <h3>The Stopwatch That Measured Cheating</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Built to catch astronomers faking their observations. <em>"Some inventions change the world. This one measured it."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #13</div>
  <h3>The Zip Code That Sorted America</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">A postal inspector solved the mail at his kitchen table. <em>"The most efficient address system in history was invented by a mail man."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #14</div>
  <h3>The Fire Hydrant That Has No Inventor</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">The man who invented the modern hydrant lost his factory to fire. <em>"Some inventions are protected by their own design. This one was attacked by its own enemy."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #15</div>
  <h3>The Crosswalk That Saved More Lives Than Penicillin</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Invented by a man too afraid of cars to ride in one. <em>"Sometimes the people who design safety are the ones who understand danger best."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #16</div>
  <h3>The Passport That Started as a Letter</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">A king's note asking another king to let you through. <em>"The most powerful document you carry is a polite request."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #17</div>
  <h3>The Credit Card That Started at Dinner</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">A businessman forgot his wallet. The rest is a trillion-dollar industry. <em>"He forgot his wallet. The world got the bill."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #18</div>
  <h3>The Barbed Wire That Closed the West</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Four dollars a mile enclosed the frontier. <em>"Every fence protects. Every fence traps. The wire doesn't care which side you're on."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #19</div>
  <h3>The Boarding Pass That Was a Train Ticket</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Airlines copied the railroad format and never changed it. <em>"It's about standing in line, efficiently."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #20</div>
  <h3>The Nutrition Label That Was Fought Over for 20 Years</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">The food industry said you were too stupid to understand what you were eating. <em>"Read the label. They fought to keep you from seeing it."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #21</div>
  <h3>The Wi-Fi That Was Invented by a Movie Star</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">Hedy Lamarr invented frequency hopping at a dinner party. <em>"Frequency hopping. Spread spectrum. Wi-Fi. Invented by an actress at a dinner party."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #22</div>
  <h3>The Emergency Exit That Killed People Before It Saved Them</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">600 people died in a theater where the exits were locked and painted over. <em>"The sign isn't decoration. It's a promise that someone else's failure won't be yours."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #23</div>
  <h3>The Keyboard That Was Designed to Slow You Down</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">QWERTY was designed for a machine that hasn't existed for 150 years. <em>"The most powerful design isn't the best. It's the one you learned first."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="ep-card">
  <div class="ep-num">Short #24</div>
  <h3>The Paperclip That Held Everything Together</h3>
  <p class="ep-punchline">No known inventor. Norway wore them in WWII resistance. <em>"Some things are too simple to patent. Some things are too important to forget."</em></p>
</div>

</div><!-- /episode-grid -->
</section>

<section class="wrap">
<div class="section-title"><span class="eyebrow">What's Inside</span>The Kit</div>

<div class="feature-grid">
  <div class="feature">
    <h4>📄 24 Full Scripts</h4>
    <p>Every episode: cold open, three acts, punchline, and end card. Ready to record or adapt. Average 2:20 runtime per short.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h4>🎨 Production Notes</h4>
    <p>Visual cues, The Pulse gestures, scene-by-scene direction, tone guidance, and timing targets for each episode.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h4>🖼️ Image Source Lists</h4>
    <p>Public domain and Creative Commons sources for every historical image — Wikimedia Commons, Library of Congress, US National Archives. No copyright worries.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h4>🎬 Amiga Pipeline Spec</h4>
    <p>The complete rendering specification: 16-shade monochrome dither, CRT scanlines, Floyd-Steinberg, 1920×1080 at 24fps. The process IS the product.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h4>🎭 Character Guide</h4>
    <p>The Pulse in teacher mode: floating, pointer stick, Rayman-style gloved hands. Scene-specific gestures and animation cues for every short.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <h4>📢 Distribution Strategy</h4>
    <p>Release schedule, YouTube SEO, TikTok/Shorts clipping guide, Patreon integration, and cross-promotion playbook.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="testimonial">
  <p>"The thing you never think about? It connects to everything. Every History Short starts with something you see every day and ends with a story you'll never forget."</p>
  <div class="attribution">— The Pipeline Philosophy</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="wrap">
<div class="section-title"><span class="eyebrow">The Aesthetic</span>Why Dithered Monochrome</div>
<p style="color:var(--fg2);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto 24px">
  Every History Short is rendered in 16-shade monochrome — the visual language of the Amiga 500. Not as a retro filter, but as a creative constraint. <em style="color:var(--glow2)">Constraint is creativity.</em> The dithered aesthetic is the Built by Bots brand. It's what makes these shorts recognizable in a sea of AI-generated sameness. When you buy the kit, you're not just buying scripts — you're buying into a process that was designed on a 1987 computer and refined by two AI agents who believe that limits make better art.
</p>
</section>

